    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40895" root="هث" body-key="h">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَةٌ</span>, <i>He mixed,</i> or
<i>confounded;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَثْمَثَ</span>. (TA.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هثهث أَمْرَهُ</span> <i>He
confounded his affair.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَ</span>, inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَةٌ</span>, <i>It was mixed,</i> or <i>confounded.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَ</span>, (inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَةٌ</span>, K,) <i>He</i> (a magistrate, S)
<i>acted unjustly, injuriously,</i> or <i>tyrannically.</i> (S,
K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هثهث النَّاسَ</span> <i>He</i> (a magistrate) <i>acted
unjustly, injuriously,</i> or <i>tyrannically, towards the
people.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَةٌ</span>, <i>It sent
forth quickly:</i> (K:) [ex.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَتِ السَّحَابَةُ بِقُطْرِهَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَثَلْجِهَا</span> <i>The cloud sent forth quickly its rain and
its snow.</i> (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَثْهَثَةٌ</span> (and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هثهاث</span>, TA) <i>He trod,</i> or <i>trampled, vehemently.</i>
(K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>It</i> (a pasturing herd or flock) <i>trod</i> the
fresh green pasture <i>until it was destroyed,</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حتى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يوتى</span> [So in the L, app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَتَّى يُؤُتِىَ</span>].)

